@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps_landscape.component.pass_rate_filter a ds:Component;
    ds:name "Pass Rate Filter";
    ds:summary "Composes a custom `TableFilter` with a Formik range form backed by the `passRateFrom` and `passRateTo` page parameters. Its badge counts bounds that differ from the URL defaults of 0 and 100; Reset writes those defaults immediately, while Apply writes the current valid form values.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "node:\n  uri: ds:apps_landscape.component.pass_rate_filter\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        uri: ds:apps_landscape.pattern.table_filter\n        role: custom filter disclosure\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: Pass rate toggle label\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.badge\n                    role: active-bound count\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                      condition: passRateFrom is greater than 0 or passRateTo is less than 100\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n          - node:\n              semantic: form\n              role: pass-rate range form\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.input\n                    role: minimum pass rate\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    role: minimum percent suffix\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.input\n                    role: maximum pass rate\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    role: maximum percent suffix\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.button\n                    role: reset action\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.button\n                    role: apply action\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"";
    ds:anatomyClassic "https://www.figma.com/design/I4WpvwMuQI6v1qhgUl63Sx/Landscape-Pragma-components?node-id=25-78&t=iG2ObZ6Q1XG2A2MB-4\n\nTable 41\n\n";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\n**Filter by a percentage range**\n\nUse for result sets whose pass rate is represented by inclusive lower and upper values on a fixed 0-100 scale.\n\n**Persist range in the URL**\n\nUse only where the shared page-parameter manager’s `passRateFrom` and `passRateTo` keys are the intended source of truth.\n\n### When not to use\n\n**Choose one threshold**\n\nA workflow that requires selecting only a minimum or maximum value, not a range.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using Pass Rate Filter to constrain input when a single numeric bound is the actual requirement.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use a single `Input` with type `\"number\"` and appropriate `min`/`max` constraints, or use a single-value slider component if visual range selection is preferred.\n\n**Edit a non-percentage range**\n\nA domain-specific control problem where the valid values are not 0-100 or percent units.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Adapting Pass Rate Filter for temperature ranges, price bands, or other non-percentage scales.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Use a domain-specific range control designed for the actual numeric scale and units. For percentage ranges outside 0-100, reconsider the UX or build a custom range component.\n\n**Reusable controlled range input**\n\nA use case where the range component must accept values and callbacks as props rather than being coupled to page parameters.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Wrapping Pass Rate Filter and trying to pass custom `from` and `to` values as props to override the page-parameter binding.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Build a controlled range component that accepts `min`, `max`, `onChange`, and `onReset` props. Alternatively, use a generic range slider library or Canonical’s form components directly.";
    ds:guidelines "### Accessibility\n\n- Canonical `Input` supplies visible `From` and `To` labels, native number inputs, and field error rendering through `getFormikError`.\n- HTML `min` and `max` attributes mirror the current opposite bound, while Yup supplies validation messages after Formik interaction.\n- Apply is a native submit button disabled when `formik.isValid` is false; Reset is a native `type=\"button\"`.\n- The adjacent percent signs are plain text and are not locally connected to the inputs with `aria-describedby` or an accessible unit label.\n\n### Content\n\n- Visible copy is fixed to `Pass rate`, `From`, `To`, `%`, `Reset`, and `Apply`, plus hard-coded Yup validation messages.\n- Badge state is computed directly: From greater than 0 adds one and To less than 100 adds one. Values outside those comparisons do not increase the badge count further.\n- Reset writes exactly 0 and 100; it does not call Formik’s `resetForm` directly.\n\n### Internationalization\n\n- All labels, actions, units, and validation messages are hard-coded in English. The component exposes no translation or content props.\n- Number parsing and formatting are delegated to the browser number input and Yup; no locale-specific display formatting is applied.\n\n### Keyboard\n\n- DOM order is From, To, Reset, Apply. Enter submits the Formik form when normal form semantics permit and validation succeeds.\n- The component adds no custom arrow-key, focus-opening, focus-return, or Escape behavior; menu behavior comes from `TableFilter`/Canonical `ContextualMenu`.\n\n### Device and layout\n\n- The form uses fixed `13rem` input widths, horizontal input/suffix rows, side padding, and right-aligned actions separated by a top border.\n- No media query or narrow-width variant is defined locally; consumers should verify the custom menu can accommodate the fixed field width.";
    ds:tier ds:apps_landscape;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.specialadoption-docs.
